#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0329 expect=skipped domain=TE
#note "AUTHORED BY Plan B phase 4d. CDISC-CG0329 had NO column-absence scenario at all before this: its only skipped fixture (-skipped_non_te_primary-DM) is a Scope.Domains gate, not a requirement gate. NEITHER TEENRL nor TEDUR is declared here, so Requirements.Variables.Any [TEENRL, TEDUR] is unmet and the rule SKIPS instead of folding dataset-constant TRUE and emitting one finding at row 1. The all-absent case is nothing-to-check, not a defect (M2-D24 / M3-F.1). DIRECTION PIN: read with -invalid_teenrl_absent-TE, authored alongside this file for exactly that purpose -- with only TEENRL withheld the Any leg is still satisfied and the rule must FIRE. Were the Any leg wired as a conjunction (skip as soon as ANY entry is absent) that sibling would go SKIPPED and RED; were the leg dropped altogether this file would fire and go RED. Neither file alone pins the direction, which is why the pair was authored together. The Check is byte-identical to CDISC-CG0328's, CORE-000027's, FDA-SD0089's and PMDA-SD0089's. Both findings snapshots are structurally blind (te.json and phuse's te.xpt each carry both columns) -- Gate C evidence."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset TE label="Trial Elements"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col ETCD    type=Char label="Element Code"
col ELEMENT type=Char label="Description of Element"
col TESTRL  type=Char label="Rule for Start of Element"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | TE | SCRN | Screening | Informed consent
CDISCPILOT01 | TE | TRT  | Treatment | First dose
